From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kodi-iris contributors <kodi-iris@invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:30:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] v4l2_m2m: discard empty error capture buffers instead of
 outputting them

Symptom: every VP9 bitexact case failed with "capture: driver decode
error" and 102 (nv12) / 105-109 (drm) frames for 100 in the stream,
first difference at frame 11.

iris_driver returns the capture buffer used for a hidden VP9 frame
(show_frame=0, the alt-ref in a superframe) with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR,
bytesused 0 and timestamp 0. get_qbuf() only treats an empty buffer as
EOS when it is not flagged as an error, so these were converted into
frames with stale buffer contents, no pts and decode_error_flags set.
Measured on vp9_640x360: 108 frames out, the 8 error ones all empty and
untimed; the remaining 100 are bit-exact against libavcodec vp9.

An empty buffer holds no picture whatever the driver, so requeue it and
dequeue the next one; error buffers with a payload are still returned
(flagged corrupt) as before. ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame() becomes a
for loop so the skip does not run xlat_pts_frame_out() on a stale frame.

Verified: tests/run-matrix.sh all 27 cases PASS (VP9 nv12+drm 4/4 each,
no regressions in H.264/HEVC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libavcodec/v4l2_context.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
index cf4b90155e..8be37aafed 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
@@ -1054,14 +1054,30 @@ int ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame(V4L2Context* ctx, AVFrame* frame, int timeout)
     V4L2Buffer *avbuf;
     int rv;
 
-    do {
+    for (;;) {
         if ((rv = get_qbuf(ctx, &avbuf, timeout)) != 0)
             return rv;
+        // A capture buffer flagged as an error with no payload holds no
+        // picture: get_qbuf() only treats an empty buffer as EOS when it is
+        // *not* an error, so these must be dropped here or stale buffer
+        // contents get output as a (corrupt, untimed) frame. iris returns the
+        // buffers of hidden VP9 frames (show_frame=0, e.g. the alt-ref in a
+        // superframe) this way. Requeue it and look for the next one.
+        if ((avbuf->buf.flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR) != 0 &&
+            (V4L2_TYPE_IS_MULTIPLANAR(ctx->type) ?
+                avbuf->buf.m.planes[0].bytesused : avbuf->buf.bytesused) == 0) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "%s: discard empty error buffer: index %d, ts=%" PRId64 ".%06ld\n",
+                   ctx->name, avbuf->buf.index,
+                   (int64_t)avbuf->buf.timestamp.tv_sec, (long)avbuf->buf.timestamp.tv_usec);
+            if ((rv = ff_v4l2_buffer_enqueue(avbuf)) != 0)
+                return rv;
+            continue;
+        }
         if ((rv = ff_v4l2_buffer_buf_to_avframe(frame, avbuf)) != 0)
             return rv;
-    } while (xlat_pts_frame_out(avctx, &s->xlat, frame) != 0);
-
-   return 0;
+        if (xlat_pts_frame_out(avctx, &s->xlat, frame) == 0)
+            return 0;
+    }
 }
 
 int ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_packet(V4L2Context* ctx, AVPacket* pkt, int timeout)
